","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,897,1405,89]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"fa4214572fd2788b6293-q-3","number":"1C","markdown":"Using Lagrange's interpolation, calculate the profit in the year 2000 from the following table:\n\n| Year | 1997 | 1999 | 2001 | 2002 |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Profit in Lakhs of ₹ | 43 | 65 | 159 | 248 |","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/fa4214572fd2788b6293/q-3-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,978,1405,186]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"fa4214572fd2788b6293-q-4","number":"2A","markdown":"Using Runge-Kutta method of order 4, solve $y' = x + y^2$ with $y(0) = 1$ at $x = 0.1, 0.2$ in steps of length $h = 0.1$.","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/fa4214572fd2788b6293/q-4-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1156,1405,104]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"fa4214572fd2788b6293-q-5","number":"2B","markdown":"Solve $(2xy + y e^x)\\,dx + (x^2 + e^x)\\,dy = 0$","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/fa4214572fd2788b6293/q-5-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1252,1405,73]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"fa4214572fd2788b6293-q-6","number":"2C","markdown":"Using Simpson's rule, evaluate\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\\int_0^1 \\frac{x^2}{1+x^3}\\,dx\n$$\n\nwith $h = 0.25$.","marks":3,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/fa4214572fd2788b6293/q-6-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1317,1405,154]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"fa4214572fd2788b6293-q-7","number":"3A","markdown":"Using Gauss elimination method, solve the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x - y + z &= 10\\\\\n2x + 4y &= 12\\\\\nx + y + 5z &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$","marks":4,"pageNumbers":[1],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/fa4214572fd2788b6293/q-7-p-1.jpg","pageNumber":1,"bbox":[0,1463,1405,171