 $y(4.1)$ and $y(4.2)$ to four decimal places, given $5x\\dfrac{dy}{dx} + y^2 - 2 = 0$ with $y(4) = 1$.","marks":5,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/fa4214572fd2788b6293/q-12-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,354,1405,122]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]},{"id":"fa4214572fd2788b6293-q-13","number":"5B","markdown":"Using Gauss-Jordan method, find the inverse of following matrix\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}\n1 & 1 & 1\\\\\n1 & -1 & 2\\\\\n3 & 1 & 1\n\\end{bmatrix}\n$$","marks":5,"pageNumbers":[2],"diagrams":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/fa4214572fd2788b6293/q-13-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,468,1405,1412],"id":"fa4214572fd2788b6293-q-13-diagram-1","caption":"Matrix A = [[1,1,1],[1,-1,2],[3,1,1]] (original source region)"}],"sourceImages":[{"src":"/repeat-v2/assets/fa4214572fd2788b6293/q-13-p-2.jpg","pageNumber":2,"bbox":[0,468,1405,1412]}],"confidence":"high","reviewNotes":[]}],"warnings":["Transcribed from original page images with gpt-5.4-mini. Automatic transcription is not independent human verification."]}
